Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] ARM: preserve Thumb state for PREL31 targets in Thumb-only PLTs

The PLT relocation fast path returns before the normal PREL31 handling.
On M-profile the PLT itself is Thumb, even if an undefined external symbol
has no Thumb function type. EHABI personality references must retain bit 0.
Otherwise the unwinder branches to Thumb PLT code in ARM state and faults.
Do not change ARM-capable PLTs or unrelated relocation types.

--- a/bfd/elf32-arm.c
+++ b/bfd/elf32-arm.c
@@ -10377,6 +10377,11 @@
 	  value = (splt->output_section->vma
 		   + splt->output_offset
 		   + plt_offset);
+	  /* PREL31 may encode an EHABI personality routine.  The
+	     fast path must retain the state of a Thumb-only PLT.  */
+	  if (r_type == R_ARM_PREL31 && using_thumb_only (globals))
+	    value |= 1;
+
 	  *unresolved_reloc_p = false;
 	  return _bfd_final_link_relocate (howto, input_bfd, input_section,
 					   contents, rel->r_offset, value,
